            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "We had a whole discussion on how to enable clang-tidy across the organization.  This is deviating from that.\n\nPlease add proposals for checks you like to the reference in docs and then use the `openbmc-build-scripts/tools/config-clang-tidy` to apply this to all the repos."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> We had a whole discussion\n\n@patrick@stwcx.xyz welcome back.  Is there something I can read?  Thanks!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Like a lot of stuff, the documentation never seemed to get fully wrapped up from the discussions...\n\n1. https://lore.kernel.org/openbmc/aDDn8JF2rvD74pvk@heinlein/ - This was the latest on the config-clang-tidy tool; the chain was Jayanth's original proposal and some discussion.\n\n2. https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/76369/9/cpp-style-and-conventions.md - Jayanth never seemed to finish this.\n\n3. There was a lot of discussion in this commit that you probably don't want to weed through.  https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/docs/+/76345\n\n4. A lot of discussion happened in this discord thread: https://discord.com/channels/775381525260664832/1318185382906560544/1318185721055678565"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "If I replaced this tidy with the one in docs would that work?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> If I replaced this tidy with the one in docs would that work?\n\nYes."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Ok cool.  If I submit fixes for problems that aren't in that list will those be rejected?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> Ok cool. If I submit fixes for problems that aren't in that list will those be rejected?\n\nI don't see why as long as they aren't out of line with the standards and conventions of the project."
                }
            ],
